<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nokia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1865</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nokia is a Finnish telecommunications company that began in 1865 as a paper mill founded by Fredrik Idestam in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tampere">Tampere</a> and later merged with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a> and cable firms. Turning to electronics, it was the world's largest maker of mobile phones from 1998 until about 2011, at its peak a large share of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>'s exports. After selling its phone business to Microsoft in 2014 it concentrated on network equipment.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nokia.jpg" alt="Nokia" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: pikkuanna · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Midpoint_Nokia_Karaportti.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
